title: The SPD proposes socialization measures.
subtitle: A crisis for our coalition's stability.
tags: event
view-if: socialization_debate_seen = 0 and year = 1919 and month = 3 and spd_in_government = 1 and economic_minister_party = 'SPD'
on-arrival: socialization_debate_seen = 1; month_actions += 1
max-visits: 1

= The SPD proposes socialization measures

<img src="img/ruhr_coal.jpeg" style="width:250px;height:250px;object-fit:cover;border:5px solid #000;"> Rudolf Wissell, a member of the SPD and Economic Minister, has introduced a piece of legislation aimed at establising guidelines for nationalization of <span style="color: [+ z_colour +];">**Ge**</span><span style="color: [+ spd_colour +];">**rm**</span><span style="color: [+ ddp_colour +];">**an**</span> industries and regulation for the coal sector in the Ruhr to appease the established worker's councils created during the Revolution. This has caused tension within our party as our ministers were not informed beforehand, with some believing said legislation is an overstep of the program that we and our <span style="color: [+ z_colour +];">We</span><span style="color: [+ spd_colour +];">im</span><span style="color: [+ ddp_colour +];">ar</span> coalition partners has agreed upon, and many of our members warn agaisnt losing the support of the middle-class if we were to support this bill.

One of our Pazifisten wing's leading spokesman, Anton Erkelenz has argued for a vote for the law and to let the DDP commit to the <span style="color: [+ kpd_colour +];">socialisation</span> of <span style="color: [+ z_colour +];">**Ge**</span><span style="color: [+ spd_colour +];">**rm**</span><span style="color: [+ ddp_colour +];">**an**</span> industries, so that the DDP could reach out towards the worker's, also arguing that it was necessary for the welfare of the people.

Whilst on the right, specifically the Nationalliberale wing and a few business Linksliberale members, few actually called for voting against the piece of legislation, fearing the coalition would collapse merely 1 month into its formation and jeopardize the work on the new constitution. However they are however, vehemently opposed to include <span style="color: [+ kpd_colour +];">socialisation</span> policies into the program as Erkelenz proposed.

- @vote_aye_erkelenz: Go all in, vote aye and adopt Erkelenz's proposal!
- @vote_aye_coalition: We shall vote aye, for the unity of the coalition, while rejecting Erkelenz's proposal
- @abstain: We shall abstain. Surely Scheidemann will understand our position.

@vote_aye_erkelenz
subtitle: This will raise a few eyebrows across the Linksliberale wing. The Nationalliberale wing is gonna be absolutely livid if we select this.
on-arrival: constitution_leverage += 4; workers_ddp += 6*(1-dissent); old_middle_ddp -= 5*(1-dissent); new_middle_ddp -= 4*(1-dissent); nationalliberale_dissent += 10; nationalliberale_strength -= 4; linksliberale_dissent += 6 if linksliberale_dissent > 0; linksliberale_strength += 6; worker_campaign_modifier += 1; old_middle_campaign_modifier -= 1; spd_relation += 8

Our business backers and Nationalliberale members are livid at our decision to not only support this <span style="color: [+ spd_colour +];">Marxist</span> bill and to deviate even further away from the middle class. We shall hope this experimentation will carry us through the new <span style="color: [+ z_colour +];">**Ge**</span><span style="color: [+ spd_colour +];">**rma**</span><span style="color: [+ ddp_colour +];">**ny**</span>... 
  
@vote_aye_coalition
subtitle: A expected course of action.
on-arrival: constitution_leverage += 2; workers_ddp += 2*(1-dissent); old_middle_ddp -= 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_ddp -= 2*(1-dissent); nationalliberale_dissent += 5; spd_relation += 8; coalition_dissent -= 2

The expected course of action, however middle class voters still somewhat leave our party over this.

@abstain
subtitle: Will he?
on-arrival: coalition_dissent += 2; constitution_leverage -= 2; workers_ddp -= 3*(1-dissent); old_middle_ddp -= 1*(1-dissent); new_middle_ddp -= 1*(1-dissent); nationalliberale_dissent -= 4 if nationalliberale_dissent > 0; linksliberale_dissent += 6; spd_relation -= 6; z_relation -= 2

The SPD is shocked at our intrisigence! Our middle class voters still grumble, but the fallout is less, and we lose much of our popularity among the workers.

